WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.640
SCP-682 versus SCP-3922. Who would win in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.640
matchup between the indestructible&nbsp;
reptile and the TV reality filter?&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.600
3922 is a small cylinder that, when placed&nbsp;
near a television, will alter the content of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.960
any fictional material being played to&nbsp;
include a battalion of heavily armored&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.280
soldiers who proceed to arrest the characters&nbsp;
in the film and try them for their crimes.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:27.840
The Foundation introduced 3922 to security footage&nbsp;
of 682. The tape was then altered into a 72-hour&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.720
military epic in which a coalition of soldiers,&nbsp;
all played by deceased actors, attempted to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.360
terminate 682 over the course of the film. The&nbsp;
film ends with a final remaining soldier, played&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:42.720
by Patrick Swayze, alongside several gigantic&nbsp;
primates staring down 682 and preparing to duke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:48.960
it out once and for all before… a TO BE CONTINUED&nbsp;
title card is displayed! Talk about a sequel hook.

